title: binary ninja IL (LLIL MLIL HLIL)
url:   https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/bnil-overview.html
tags:  binaryninja binja bn bnil il llil mlil hlil ssa intermediate-language decompiler dataflow python api

; il = an IL function (f.llil / f.mlil / f.hlil), i = an IL instruction.
; LLIL = registers and flags, MLIL = variables and typed calls, HLIL = C-like AST.
; Most lines work at all three levels, the link shows one of them.

## get il
f.llil, f.mlil, f.hlil        # get the IL function of a Function at each level  @lowlevelil @mediumlevelil @highlevelil  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.mlil>
il.instructions               # iterate the top-level instructions  @loop @walk  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.instructions>
[i for bb in il for i in bb]  # list all instructions by walking IL blocks  @loop @cfg  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILBasicBlock>
il.basic_blocks               # list IL basic blocks  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.basic_blocks>
il[INDEX]                     # get an instruction by its instruction index  @index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction>
il.get_expr(EXPR_INDEX)       # get an expression by its expression index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_expr>
il.source_function            # get the Function that owns this IL  @owner  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.source_function>
il.ssa_form                   # get the SSA version of the IL function  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.ssa_form>
il.non_ssa_form               # go back from SSA to the normal IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.non_ssa_form>
il.root                       # get the top node of the HLIL tree  @ast  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILFunction.root>
f.get_llil_at(ADDR)           # get the LLIL instruction at a code address  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.get_llil_at>
ref.mlil                      # get the MLIL instruction at an xref (from bv.get_code_refs)  @xrefs  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.ReferenceSource.mlil>

## instruction fields
i.operation          # get the opcode enum, e.g. MediumLevelILOperation.MLIL_CALL  @opcode @kind  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.operation>
i.address            # get the native address the instruction came from  @addr  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.address>
i.instr_index        # get the instruction index in its IL function  @index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.expr_index         # get the expression index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.size               # get the operation size in bytes  @width  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.size>
i.operands           # list the operands (sub-expressions, vars, constants)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.operands>
i.detailed_operands  # list (name, value, type) for each operand, good for learning  @debug @explore  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.detailed_operands>
i.tokens             # get the text tokens of the instruction  @print @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.tokens>
str(i)               # get the instruction as text  @print  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.il_basic_block     # get the IL block that holds the instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.il_basic_block>
i.function           # get the IL function of the instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.expr_type          # get the type of an MLIL or HLIL expression  @typeof  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.expr_type>
i.parent             # get the parent node in the HLIL tree  @ast @up  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.parent>
i.lines              # get the HLIL lines for this node  @print @decompile  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.lines>

## match by class
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILCall)          # test for a call; i.dest target, i.params args, i.output results  @call @args  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILCall>
isinstance(i, HighLevelILCall)            # test for an HLIL call; i.dest is the target, i.params the args  @call @args  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILCall>
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILSetVar)        # test for "var = expr"; i.dest is the Variable, i.src the expression  @assign  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILSetVar>
isinstance(i, HighLevelILAssign)          # test for an HLIL assignment; i.dest and i.src  @assign  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILAssign>
isinstance(i, HighLevelILVarInit)         # test for an HLIL declaration with a value "int x = ..."  @assign @declare  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILVarInit>
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILIf)            # test for a branch; i.condition, i.true and i.false indexes  @branch @condition  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILIf>
isinstance(i, HighLevelILIf)              # test for an HLIL if; i.condition, i.true and i.false bodies  @branch @condition  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILIf>
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILStore)         # test for a memory write "[dest] = src"  @write @pointer  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILStore>
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILLoad)          # test for a memory read "[src]"  @read @deref  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILLoad>
isinstance(i, Constant)                   # test for any constant at any level; i.constant is the value  @immediate @number  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Constant>
isinstance(i, Call)                       # test for any call at any level (Call, Tailcall, Syscall)  @call  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Call>
isinstance(i, Return)                     # test for any return instruction  @ret  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Return>
isinstance(i, Load), isinstance(i, Store)  # test for memory access at any level  @memory  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Load>
isinstance(i, BinaryOperation)            # test for any two-operand op; i.left and i.right  @arithmetic @add @xor  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.BinaryOperation>
isinstance(i, Comparison)                 # test for a compare (==, <, ...); i.left and i.right  @cmp  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Comparison>
isinstance(i, Phi)                        # test for an SSA phi node  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Phi>
i.operation == MediumLevelILOperation.MLIL_CALL  # test the opcode enum instead of the class  @opcode  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.enums-module.html#binaryninja.enums.MediumLevelILOperation>
match i: case MediumLevelILCall(dest=MediumLevelILConstPtr(constant=c)):  # match a direct call to a known address  @match @call  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILConstPtr>

## walk sub-expressions
il.traverse(FN)      # call FN(expr) on every expression, yield the non-None results  @visit @walk @search  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.traverse>
    def find_calls(e):
        if isinstance(e, HighLevelILCall): return e
    for c in f.hlil.traverse(find_calls): print(hex(c.address), c)
i.traverse(FN, ARG)  # walk one instruction's tree, extra args go to FN(expr, ARG)  @visit @walk  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.traverse>
il.visit(FN)         # call FN(name, expr, type, parent) on each node, return False to stop descending  @walk  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.visit>
i.prefix_operands    # list the instruction tree flattened in prefix order  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.prefix_operands>
i.postfix_operands   # list the instruction tree flattened in postfix order  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.postfix_operands>

## move between levels
i.llil, i.mlil, i.hlil         # get the matching instruction at another level, or None  @map @convert  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.hlil>
i.llils, i.mlils, i.hlils      # list all matching instructions at another level  @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.hlils>
i.ssa_form                     # get the SSA version of an instruction  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.ssa_form>
i.non_ssa_form                 # get the normal version of an SSA instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.non_ssa_form>
f.llil.mapped_medium_level_il  # get MLIL that keeps a 1:1 map to LLIL  @mmlil  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.mapped_medium_level_il>

## variables and def-use
i.vars_read                         # list variables an MLIL or HLIL instruction reads  @use  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.vars_read>
i.vars_written                      # list variables an instruction writes  @def @assign  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.vars_written>
il.vars                             # list variables used in the IL function  @locals  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.vars>
il.get_var_definitions(VAR)         # list instructions that assign VAR  @def @defs  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_var_definitions>
il.get_var_uses(VAR)                # list instructions that read VAR  @use @uses  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_var_uses>
il.ssa_vars                         # list SSA variables (var + version)  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.ssa_vars>
il.get_ssa_var_definition(SSA_VAR)  # get the one instruction that defines an SSA var  @ssa @def  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_definition>
il.get_ssa_var_uses(SSA_VAR)        # list instructions that use an SSA var  @ssa @use  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_uses>
il.get_ssa_var_value(SSA_VAR)       # get the dataflow value of an SSA var  @ssa @constant  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_value>
SSAVariable(VAR, VERSION)           # make an SSA variable to look up  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.SSAVariable>
i.get_var_for_reg("rdi")            # get the MLIL variable that holds a register here  @register @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_var_for_reg>
i.get_ssa_var_version(VAR)          # get the SSA version of VAR at this instruction  @ssa  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_ssa_var_version>

## dataflow values
i.value                             # get the known value of an expression (RegisterValue)  @constant @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.value>
i.value.type, i.value.value         # check value kind (ConstantValue, StackFrameOffset...) and the number  @constant  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.variable-module.html#binaryninja.variable.RegisterValue>
i.possible_values                   # get the set or range of values an expression can have  @range @dataflow @switch  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.possible_values>
i.get_reg_value("rax")              # get the known register value before this instruction  @register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_reg_value>
i.get_reg_value_after("rax")        # get the known register value after this instruction  @register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_reg_value_after>
i.get_stack_contents(OFFSET, SIZE)  # get the known stack value at an offset  @stack  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_stack_contents>
i.branch_dependence                 # get which branches decide whether this instruction runs  @control-dependence  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.branch_dependence>

## llil specifics
isinstance(i, LowLevelILSetReg)           # test for "reg = expr"; i.dest register, i.src value  @assign @register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILSetReg>
i.get_flag_value("z")                     # get the known flag value before this instruction  @flags @zf  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILInstruction.get_flag_value>
il.regs                                   # list registers used in the LLIL function  @register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.regs>
il.get_instructions_at(ADDR)              # list LLIL instructions for a native address  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_instructions_at>
bv.arch.get_low_level_il_from_bytes(DATA, ADDR)  # lift raw bytes to LLIL without a function  @lift  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.architecture-module.html#binaryninja.architecture.Architecture.get_low_level_il_from_bytes>

## modify il (in workflows)
il.replace_expr(OLD, NEW)              # swap an expression for another one  @patch @rewrite  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.replace_expr>
il.copy_expr(EXPR)                     # copy an expression into this IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.copy_expr>
il.translate(FN)                       # build a new IL function by mapping each expression through FN  @rewrite @transform  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.translate>
il.finalize(); il.generate_ssa_form()  # finish editing and rebuild SSA  @rewrite  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.finalize>
il.create_graph()                      # build a FlowGraph of the IL  @cfg @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.create_graph>
